        Root cause:
        The bug was caused by incorrect parsing of Kerberos principal names, specifically the failure to correctly extract the realm from the principal string, leading to improper handling of HTTP SPNEGO principals within the authentication process. This resulted in the inability to accurately map server principals, which could lead to authentication failures in a Kerberos-secured environment.

